  "findings": [
    "Private instrumentation regressed N2-N3 communication. Normal firmware restored that pair; no production firmware changes were adopted.",
    "During A1 and B, both USB nodes accepted N1 polls but no completed ranges. N3 accepted no N2 poll. Successful TX completion does not establish valid transmitted RF content.",
    "Observed last RX status 0000af70 includes RF FCS failure, not a reported SPI CRC error. It is sticky and is not an error count for every later attempt.",
    "No observed SPI CRC/status or duplicate-timestamp mismatches during the settled probe counter intervals. This does not exclude deterministic timestamp, transfer or first-path errors.",
    "No successful six-timestamp hardware trace was captured; physical timestamp correctness remains untested. Offline replay self-tests only establish arithmetic consistency.",
    "N1 traffic ceased before A2 and remained absent after restore and a later passive8s check. Power loss, MCU stall and radio stall cannot be distinguished remotely.",
    "The new wall-duration guard rejects sleep/clock-interrupted browser and CLI recordings while preserving raw data. Earlier recordings without wall time require separate timing evidence."
  ],
  "next_controlled_step": "When all three nodes are available again, isolate the private CRC path while retaining the other instrumentation, verify a baseline without host sleep, and preserve settings. A CRC-off variant must ignore SPICRCE and change CRC init validation. No new offset fitting.",
